  "question": {
    "text": "The positive value of parameter <math><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the area bounded by parabolas <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> attains the maximum value is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Points of intersection are at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8747;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mi>dx</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><br />Hence, area is maximum when&nbsp;<math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>"
  }
